  "kerberos_call_chain": [
    "libkrb5 localauth_rule.an2ln_rule -> aname_do_match/aname_replacer -> regcomp/regexec",
    "krb5_aname_to_localname or krb5_kuserok -> local authorization module -> RULE callback",
    "libgssapi krb5_gss_localname or krb5_gss_authorize_localname -> the above local authorization entry points"
  ],
  "reviewed_client_boundary": "PostgreSQL18.6 libpq client uses only the eleven measured client GSS APIs. All33 client C/H sources contain no localname/userok API or symbol-name lookup. The Kerberos mechanism registers localname/authorization callbacks separately from its client init/acquire/wrap paths. The affected local-authorization path is not selected by these client APIs, including when libpq gssencmode is prefer and GSS is used.",
  "not_a_password_configuration_exception": true,
  "libc_cleanup_boundary": "libc_malloc_debug.so.0 imports __libc_freeres. Its __libc_regcomp_freemem hook can call __regfree on the shared BSD regex buffer; it is not claimed uncalled. That buffer is initialized only by re_comp, and no current client/API/FFI entry selects re_comp. Thus this cleanup hook does not establish a reachable preceding damaged BSD DFA state.",
  "downstream_patch_review": "The exact CentOS SRPM has no patch to localauth_rule.c or its regcomp/regexec calls. The patch touching gssapi_krb5.c only adds a separate SASL-SSF inquiry OID handler; it does not change the localname/authorization callbacks or add a client call to them.",
  "uninstalled_source_targets": "Other SRPM regcomp/regexec uses belong to kadmin server/tools or PKINIT plugin source. None of their ELF paths is installed in this exact runtime closure.",
  "invalidation": [
    "New native/Python bytes; new FFI path; calling GSS localname/authorization or direct POSIX regex APIs; loading external Kerberos/GSS plugins; changing the application client-only boundary requires renewed review."
  ],
  "remaining": "Independent complete Python FFI/dynamic lookup and libc-internal entry-point reviews must also support this decision. No proof is based only on absent imports or the local .env password."
}
